think Read recursion-prompts/patchouli-inner.md whole. It asks each lap to re-run the header nets fresh rather than trust the prior reading, and to check in when the queue stays empty.
think Pulled xy main first: two commits behind, a rebase with no conflict, HEAD now 2b76a9bd70. The round-open came before any read, so the nets below describe this tree rather than the stale one.
think Ran the two nets over all of mantra/ and tally/. The elder read-compat headers (mantra-weave-v1/v2, mantra-commit-v1) are the strings the naming law keeps forever. The witness print labels and fixture-signature constants are test identifiers, not persisted headers. No new candidate.
think Read the OPEN and BOOKED rows of construction/REDS.md. None names mantra/ or tally/ as agent-doable: %807 wants Keaton's ruling on the head-insert refusal, %765's remaining families sit in other lanes, and the rest name other owners.
think The claim board reads verdict=board, board=upstream, claims_live=0, commits_behind=2 before the pull. No peer holds this lane, so there is nothing to honor and nothing to open.
obs The queue has now read empty three times today on this shelf. A fourth identical sweep would only add a log, so this lap records the fresh nets and stops.
obs The inner prompt's own rule covers this case: when the scan finds no header, the lap says the queue is empty and stops. Nothing here calls for a claim-as-override, because the open rows all carry an owner.
rota rota lap 9838, row 3 -- Water, the row that tastes; the taste is the same as this morning's: the lane has said empty, and the honest move is one plain sentence rather than another sweep.
